#
# The POSITIVE control for `mf:include`: a pure aggregator, exactly the shape the
# vendored SEP-0009 corpus uses in `vectors/sparql-cdt/manifest-all.ttl` — zero
# `mf:entries`, one `mf:include` collection of group manifests. Loading it must
# yield the union of its children's cases; before `mf:include` was implemented it
# yielded ZERO cases and reported success, which is the silent green this fixture
# exists to keep closed.
#
# Named `manifest-all.ttl`, not `manifest.ttl`: the datatest root glob in
# `crates/sparql-conformance/tests/sparql_conformance.rs` discovers every
# `*/manifest.ttl`, so an aggregator with that name would be discovered alongside
# the children it includes and every child case would run twice. `manifest::load`
# refuses that shape by name (see `include-named-manifest/` below this directory).
#
# The whole tree lives under `tests/fixtures/`, never under `suite/`, so nothing
# here is ever picked up as a live conformance case.
@prefix mf: <http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/DataAccess/tests/test-manifest#> .

<> a mf:Manifest ;
    mf:include (
        <alpha/manifest.ttl>
        <beta/manifest.ttl>
    ) .
